==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* [[borborigmus]]

===Etymology===
From Greek [[βορβορυγμος]] ''([[onomatopoeia]])''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bɔːbəˈrɪɡməs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|borborygmi}}

# A [[rumbling]] sound made by the [[movement]] of [[gas]] in the [[intestines]].
# Something resembling borborygmus, taken in a figurative sense.
#* '''1991''', Rebecca Goldstein, ''The Dark Sister'', Penguin Books, p.36:
#*: Finally, the emotional borborygmus subsiding, she produced, at last, the words: "It is said Bonnet." 

